            "style": "box",
            "title": "How does the glow work on your glowstone rings?",
            "content": "<p>The glow comes from strontium aluminate, which is a natural crystal powder that glows after being charged with a UV light. It is nontoxic and glows brighter and longer than copper activated zinc sulfide, which is one of its most popular competitors. Check out our blog post on<a href=\"https://patrickadairdesigns.com/blogs/blog/how-to-get-your-glow-ring-to-glow\" title=\"https://patrickadairdesigns.com/blogs/blog/how-to-get-your-glow-ring-to-glow\"><strong>How Our Glow Rings Glow</strong></a> for more information on how to charge and how long they glow for</p>",
            "page": "",
            "enable_readmore": false,
            "size_chart": ""
          }
        },
        "tab_NpDk3y": {
          "type": "tab",
          "settings": {
            "expanded": true,
            "style": "box",
            "title": "What is Damascus Steel?",
            "content": "<p>Damascus steel is created by combining strips of either iron and steel or two different kinds of steel. They are then heated and forged to create a new and stronger steel. The material has a similar silver color; however, if it is placed in an acid bath, the acid will eat at the different combinations of steel at different rates to form a woodgrain pattern that makes <a href=\"https://patrickadairdesigns.com/collections/damascus-steel-rings\" target=\"_self\"><strong>Damascus Steel Rings </strong></a>incredibly unique.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": "",
            "enable_readmore": false,
